# Updating these rules

These `.mdc` files are a snapshot of the briefing pack and the current app. Edit them when the docs, protos, or implemented conventions change. They are not more authoritative than the sources.

## Documentation-first (mandatory)

Before a non-trivial task, follow `.cursor/rules/workflow.mdc` end-to-end:

1. Identify and read relevant `docs/` (and `../new-hires` when APIs are involved).
2. Read applicable `.cursor/rules/`.
3. Inspect existing code; search for reusable patterns.
4. Make the smallest change that extends the current architecture.
5. Update documentation automatically when architecture, API, auth, routing, state, infrastructure, or conventions change — do not wait to be asked.
6. Verify with the smallest relevant command and report honestly.

Distinguish **CURRENT IMPLEMENTATION**, **PROJECT STANDARD**, and **PLANNED** behavior. Never document plans as shipped.

## Read first when editing rules or BFF docs

- `../new-hires/docs/bff-connect-client.md` — transport, codegen, auth
- `../new-hires/docs/architecture-and-design-genai-lunaya-flow/index.md` — system split, maturity
- `../new-hires/docs/architecture-and-design-genai-lunaya-flow/product-workflows-actions-bff-gui-integration-guide.md` — canvas RPCs, permissions, JSON shape
- `../new-hires/proto/genius/**/*.proto` — RPC and field names
- `docs/architecture.md` and `.cursor/rules/architecture.mdc` — folder placement. Update both together when structure changes.
- `docs/backend/` — frontend reading of the BFF. Update it when `../new-hires` protos or integration docs change. Protos win on shape.

If a doc and a `.proto` disagree, follow the proto for request/response shape and note the conflict in the rule you update.
